:name: bt2usb-sim
:description: SoftDevice-free bt2usb firmware running on a simulated nRF52840.

# ── What this does ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Boots the `bt2usb-sim` binary (built with `--features sim`) on Renode's
# bundled nRF52840 model, with its GPIO/GPIOTE swapped for models that
# implement pin SENSE/LATCH and the GPIOTE PORT event (renode/*.cs, *.repl) so
# injected button edges reach the firmware. The firmware reuses the real GPIO
# button driver and the host-tested UI/coordinator logic, driven by a synthetic
# BLE scenario plus the buttons you press. Human-readable output goes to UART0.
#
# Build the ELF first:
#   mask sim-build   (cargo build --features sim --target thumbv7em-none-eabihf)
#
# Interactive run (opens a UART terminal window in the Renode GUI), from the
# repository root:
#   renode renode/bt2usb-sim.resc
#
# Press a button in the monitor. Buttons are active-low (pulled up): drive the
# pin low to press, high to release. SELECT = 24, DOWN = 12, UP = 11 (P0.xx):
#   gpio0 OnGPIO 24 false     # press SELECT
#   gpio0 OnGPIO 24 true      # release SELECT
#
# Headless / CI run (asserts the output, no GUI):
#   renode-test renode/bt2usb-sim.robot
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ELF path; override with:  renode -e "$bin=@/abs/path" renode/bt2usb-sim.resc
$bin ?= @target/thumbv7em-none-eabihf/debug/bt2usb-sim

using sysbus

# GPIO/GPIOTE models with pin SENSE/LATCH + GPIOTE PORT event (compiled here).
include @renode/nrf52840_sense_gpio.cs

mach create "bt2usb-sim"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/nrf52840.repl
# Swap the stock GPIO/GPIOTE (no SENSE/LATCH, no PORT event) for the models above.
sysbus Unregister sysbus.gpiote
sysbus Unregister sysbus.gpio0
sysbus Unregister sysbus.gpio1
machine LoadPlatformDescription @renode/nrf52840-sense-gpio.repl

# Show UART0 output (the firmware's log) in a terminal window.
showAnalyzer sysbus.uart0

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $bin
"""
runMacro $reset

echo ""
echo "bt2usb-sim loaded. UART0 output (coordinator + UI logic) appears in the"
echo "analyzer window once started. The BLE scenario runs on its own; press the"
echo "buttons (active-low; SELECT=24, DOWN=12, UP=11) to drive the UI, e.g.:"
echo "    gpio0 OnGPIO 24 false     # press SELECT"
echo "    gpio0 OnGPIO 24 true      # release SELECT"
echo ""

start
